```sh ntexup``` Declarative Document & Presentation Generator

```sh ntexup``` is an open-source, text-based document and presentation generator designed to make the creation of professional, math-heavy, and reusable teaching materials effortless.

### INSTALL

```
nuts install ntexup
```

##) EXAMPLE OF USAGE

```
nuts ntexup --view  file.ntexup
```

###) SYNOPSYS (CMD MODE)

```
nuts ntexup <option> file.ntexup
```

Options are :

```--reopen```
reopen last file/folder

```--build-repo --dump```
build repository

```--list-templates```
list available templates

```--documentation```
build documentation

```--open=<path>```
generate file ntexup file/folder

```--output=<path>```
generated file output file/folder path


```--pdf```
generate pf

```--dump```
show dump


###) SYNOPSYS (UI MODE)

```
nuts ntexup --view <option>
```


Options are :

```--new```
open new project

```--view-log```
show log panel


```--documentation```
show documentation

```--open <path>```


##) EXAMPLES:

# ntexup: generate pdf
nuts -Zy -w test ntexup myfolder
